of the taxable REIT subsidiary if (1)&nbsp;at least 90% of the property is leased to unrelated lessees and the rent paid by the taxable REIT subsidiary is substantially comparable to the rent paid by the unrelated lessees for comparable space or
(2)&nbsp;the property is a &#147;qualified lodging facility&#148; or a &#147;qualified health care facility&#148; and certain additional requirements are satisfied. </P></TD></TR></TABLE>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Unless we determine that the resulting nonqualifying income under any of the following situations, taken together with all other nonqualifying
income earned by us in the taxable year, will not jeopardize our status as a REIT, we do not intend to: </P> <P STYLE="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
