 <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Plan Assets are defined in Section&nbsp;3(42) of ERISA. The DOL has promulgated a final
regulation under ERISA, 29 C.F.R. &#167; 2510.3-101, or the Plan Assets Regulation, that provides guidelines as to whether, and under what circumstances, the underlying assets of an entity will be deemed to constitute Plan Assets for purposes of
applying the fiduciary requirements of Title I of ERISA (including the prohibited transaction rules of Section&nbsp;406&nbsp;of ERISA) and the prohibited transaction provisions of Code Section&nbsp;4975. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Under the Plan Assets Regulation, the assets of an entity in which a Plan makes an equity investment will generally be deemed to be assets of
