whether an investment in our shares is appropriate for, and permissible under, the terms of its IRA governing documents. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Although IRAs
are not subject to ERISA, as discussed above, they are subject to the provisions of Section&nbsp;4975 of the Code, prohibiting transactions with &#147;disqualified persons&#148; and investments and transactions involving fiduciary conflicts. A
